From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:17:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: take the card from logind

The card was the one device the browser opened itself. It now comes from
`Session.TakeDevice` on the connection that holds control of the
session, like every keyboard and mouse.

- `DrmLogindSession` takes control of the session in `InitializeUI`,
  before the card is opened and before the evdev thread starts. logind
  accepts `TakeDevice` only from the connection that called
  `TakeControl`, so the cards and `DrmLogindInput` share it.
- `OpenDrmDevice` takes each card from it. A relaunched GPU process
  releases and retakes the primary card; a removed card is given back.
- logind drops DRM master on a console switch and sets it again on the
  way back, so the browser keeps no `dup` and makes no master ioctls.
  `DrmMaster` is gone.
- logind drops master before the browser hears of the switch. A flip in
  between fails; `HardwareDisplayController` checks the kernel
  (`DrmWrapper::HoldsMaster`) and skips it instead of arming
  `PageFlipWatchdog`, which would kill the GPU process 15 s later.
- `DrmLogindSession` waits on logind from the UI thread, so it is a
  friend of `ScopedAllowBaseSyncPrimitivesOutsideBlockingScope`.

`HardwareDisplayControllerTest.AFlipAfterLogindTookMasterIsSkipped`
covers the skipped flip.
